# Brand kit: source files, fonts and print masters. The site copy of the email logo lives in images/brand/.
# Anchored with a leading slash: a bare "brand/" also matches media/brand/ and images/brand/,
# which the live site needs (logos, monogram, favicons, email-signature logo).
/brand/

# Internal files that must never be served as static files. Every pattern is
# anchored to the repo root, so it can't catch a same-named file the site uses
# deeper down. Keep lib/ and api/ (the functions need them), package.json and
# vercel.json (the build needs them).
#   SQL migrations and seeds (one held an admin password), internal system docs,
#   the local dev server, the SEO command-line tool (nothing in api/ or lib/
#   requires it), a copy-paste snippet that isn't a page, secrets and
#   editor/agent metadata. Root .txt files (robots.txt, the IndexNow key) stay.
/supabase/
/*.md
/server.js
/tools/
/_includes/
/.env*
/.gitignore
/.claude/
/.vscode/
/.idea/
